# Code Style

## Formatting

- Indentation: 2 spaces (no tabs)
- Quotes: single quotes for all strings (`'text'`, not `"text"`)
- Semicolons: always
- Line length: 100 characters max
- Trailing commas: ES5 style (yes in objects/arrays, no after last function param)
- Arrow parens: omit when possible (`x => x`, not `(x) => x`)
- Line endings: LF

```typescript
// CORRECT
const name = 'Stride';
const items = ['one', 'two', 'three'];
const fn = x => x * 2;

// WRONG
const name = "Stride"
const fn = (x) => x * 2
```

## Naming Conventions

| Thing | Convention | Example |
|---|---|---|
| Files (types, entities, enums) | PascalCase | `TaskStatus.ts`, `CreateTaskInput.ts` |
| Files (repos, services, hooks) | kebab-case | `task.repo.ts`, `task.service.ts`, `useSyncStatus.ts` |
| Files (React components) | PascalCase | `TaskCard.tsx`, `TodayView.tsx` |
| Files (CSS Modules) | PascalCase matching component | `Auth.module.css`, `Dashboard.module.css` |
| Classes | PascalCase | `TaskService`, `TaskRepository` |
| Instances/singletons | camelCase | `taskService`, `taskRepo` |
| Functions | camelCase | `toDomain`, `sanitizeFields` |
| React components | PascalCase function | `function TodayView()` |
| Hooks | camelCase with `use` prefix | `useAuth`, `useSyncStatus` |
| Types (domain entities) | PascalCase | `type Task = { ... }` |
| Types (inputs/DTOs) | PascalCase | `type CreateTaskInput = { ... }` |
| Enums (as const objects) | PascalCase | `const TaskStatus = { ... } as const` |
| Constants | UPPER_SNAKE_CASE | `const UNDO_TIMEOUT_MS = 10_000` |
| DB columns | camelCase TS / snake_case SQL | `firstName` maps to `first_name` |

## Import Rules

```typescript
// 1. Use `import type` for type-only imports
import type { Task, Project } from '@stridetime/types';
import type { StrideDatabase } from '@stridetime/db';

// 2. Separate value imports from type imports
import { TaskStatus, TaskDifficulty } from '@stridetime/types';
import { taskService } from '@stridetime/core';

// 3. Use alias for default repo imports in services
import {
  taskRepo as defaultTaskRepo,
  type TaskRepository,
} from '@stridetime/db';

// 4. Relative imports for same-package files
import { tasksTable } from '../drizzle/schema';
import { generateId, now } from '../db/utils';

// 5. Never import from @stridetime/db in stride-desktop (use @stridetime/core)
//    The ONLY exception is stride-desktop/src/lib/db.ts for database init
```

## Type Definitions in stride-types

**Enums — `as const` objects, NOT TypeScript `enum`:**
```typescript
// CORRECT
export const TaskPriority = {
  CRITICAL: 'CRITICAL',
  HIGH: 'HIGH',
  MEDIUM: 'MEDIUM',
  LOW: 'LOW',
  NONE: 'NONE',
} as const;
export type TaskPriority = (typeof TaskPriority)[keyof typeof TaskPriority];

// WRONG
export enum TaskPriority { CRITICAL = 'CRITICAL' }
```

**Entities — `type`, not `interface`:**
```typescript
// CORRECT
export type Task = { id: string; title: string; status: TaskStatus };

// WRONG
export interface Task { ... }
```

**Inputs/DTOs — also `type`:**
```typescript
export type CreateTaskInput = {
  title: string;
  projectId: string;
};
```

**Always use `type`, never `interface`** — for entities, inputs, props, everything.

**Exports — barrel pattern, type-only for non-enums:**
```typescript
// subdirectory index.ts
export type { Task } from './Task';        // type-only for entities
export { TaskStatus } from './TaskStatus'; // value export for enums

// src/index.ts
export type { Task, Project } from './entities';
export { TaskStatus, TaskDifficulty } from './enums';
```

**One type/enum/input per file.**
